 About Kerala Blockchain Academy 
 Kerala Blockchain Academy (KBA) a non-profit CoE in Blockchain under Digital University Kerala is India’s First Blockchain Academy in the Government Sector established by the Government of Kerala in 2017. KBA has successfully implemented the World’s first Accelerated Blockchain Competency Development (ABCD) program with Kerala Development and Innovation Strategic Council (K-DISC), training over 25000 candidates in Blockchain. Thus far, KBA h
as trained over 33500 candidates from over 66+ countries offering 13+ programs in online and offline modes. Over the years, KBA has established its relevance in the blockchain space by becoming an Associate Member and Official Training Partner of Linux Foundation’s Hyperledger Foundation, General Partner for R3 Consortium of Corda Blockchain, partner of Zilliqa Blockchain, IBF, etc to name a few. 
 The institution has established three important verticals: The Blockchain Garage &#8211; focussing on building blockchain solutions for the government and private sector; The Decentralized Lab &#8211; focussing on Blockchain R&D initiatives; and The Blockchain Powerhouse &#8211; focussing on education and capacity building. We also run KBA Innovation Clubs (KBAIC) across 83+ member institutions to support f
 The Blockchain Powerhouse has established its presence in capacity-building programs in blockchain globally, and some of the major institutions and corporates that availed blockchain programs include IIT-Kanpur, NPCI, DRDO, IMT-Dubai, BEL, Sony India, etc. The Blockchain powerhouse is actively contributing towards the education space and is making significant strides in the education sector, offerin
g a variety of online and offline courses that cater to both self-paced learners and those seeking instructor-led training. Our popular blockchain courses include the Ethereum Developer Program, Certified Hyperledger Fabric Developer, Developer Essentials for Blockchain, Certified Startup Program and Certified Blockchain Associate. 
 The Decentralized Lab is actively involved in R&D with prominent national and international research institutes. It supports research scholars in cutting-edge research in the latest Web3 approaches including Zero-Knowledge proofs (ZKP), DePIN, DAO, DeFi, etc. The researchers are actively contributing to the open-source blockchain community and toward many cutting-edge
 KBA has established a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) with several leading companies to drive advancements in blockchain technology and its applications. Our partners include UST Global, Wipro, Intel, Grant Thornton Blockchain, BIRAC, NDimensionZ Solution Pvt Ltd, Regov Techno
 Kerala Blockchain Academy (KBA) is a center of excellence under the Kerala University of Digital Sciences, Innovation and Technology. 
